{"about_the_game":"A Game Design Capstone Project - By DePaul University Students!<br><br>After returning from a star-dust-scavenging trip, Bit, our little starling captain, finds his Ship commandeered by an intergalactic militia, the Infestors. To save his home, he ventures within the circuits of his Starship friend, to rewire damage done by the Infestors and rid the circuits of malware.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/ec35903ffbff7b3a401cc62146507b49.poster.avif?t=1726073469\" width=500 height=250 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/ec35903ffbff7b3a401cc62146507b49.webm?t=1726073469\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/ec35903ffbff7b3a401cc62146507b49.mp4?t=1726073469\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >PHYSICS BASED CABLE GAMEPLAY!</h2>Star-Wired is a whimsical, endearing, top-down puzzle game, with a focus on plugging in cables to power level mechanics! The cables can be pushed, tangled, pulled, wrapped around, and swung to complete circuits and open the exit door of each level. <br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/04155cd8c0df6dec6bafe3a6c4099c26.poster.avif?t=1726073469\" width=374 height=210 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/04155cd8c0df6dec6bafe3a6c4099c26.webm?t=1726073469\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/04155cd8c0df6dec6bafe3a6c4099c26.mp4?t=1726073469\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br><strong>DEV TEAM</strong> <br><br>Liv Baughman: art lead, environment, and 2D art <br><br>Maeve Butler: 3D art and animation<br><br>Brandon Ehrman: 3D art <br><br>Tyler Ackerman: level design and gameplay programming<br><br>Catherine Simmons: producer, social media manager<br><br>Kai Langevin: lead programmer <br><br>Jake Arthur: designer, prototype<br><br><br><strong>SOUND TEAM</strong><br><br>Beth Sawltz: sound design, music<br><br>Collin Wittlich: cutscene sound effects, music","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2890990?t=1726073469","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1726073469","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1726073469","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1726073469","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Full controller support","id":28}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"controller_support":"full","detailed_description":"A Game Design Capstone Project - By DePaul University Students!<br><br>After returning from a star-dust-scavenging trip, Bit, our little starling captain, finds his Ship commandeered by an intergalactic militia, the Infestors. To save his home, he ventures within the circuits of his Starship friend, to rewire damage done by the Infestors and rid the circuits of malware.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/ec35903ffbff7b3a401cc62146507b49.poster.avif?t=1726073469\" width=500 height=250 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/ec35903ffbff7b3a401cc62146507b49.webm?t=1726073469\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/ec35903ffbff7b3a401cc62146507b49.mp4?t=1726073469\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >PHYSICS BASED CABLE GAMEPLAY!</h2>Star-Wired is a whimsical, endearing, top-down puzzle game, with a focus on plugging in cables to power level mechanics! The cables can be pushed, tangled, pulled, wrapped around, and swung to complete circuits and open the exit door of each level. <br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/04155cd8c0df6dec6bafe3a6c4099c26.poster.avif?t=1726073469\" width=374 height=210 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/04155cd8c0df6dec6bafe3a6c4099c26.webm?t=1726073469\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/extras/04155cd8c0df6dec6bafe3a6c4099c26.mp4?t=1726073469\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br><strong>DEV TEAM</strong> <br><br>Liv Baughman: art lead, environment, and 2D art <br><br>Maeve Butler: 3D art and animation<br><br>Brandon Ehrman: 3D art <br><br>Tyler Ackerman: level design and gameplay programming<br><br>Catherine Simmons: producer, social media manager<br><br>Kai Langevin: lead programmer <br><br>Jake Arthur: designer, prototype<br><br><br><strong>SOUND TEAM</strong><br><br>Beth Sawltz: sound design, music<br><br>Collin Wittlich: cutscene sound effects, music","developers":["motherbored"],"genres":[{"description":"Casual","id":"4"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"Free To Play","id":"37"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2890990/header.jpg?t=1726073469","is_free":true,"linux_requirements":[],"mac_requirements":[],"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/2890990/704646/c51a1c2278128e872963b4619285d2d026